```text
DV-1  exact dialogue wording, language, and speaker assignment remain A1 semantic/story authority
DV-2  an approved spoken rendition is an A7 Vocal Performance Revision with retained audio and exact temporal identity
DV-3  word/phoneme/viseme analysis is derived evidence from the retained vocal performance, never independent authority
DV-4  adopted facial articulation is A7 Performance authority and binds the exact source Vocal Performance Revision
DV-5  vocal, facial, and Shot-relative timing use an exact integer/rational mapping; floating seconds are not authority
DV-6  dialogue/vocal/facial replacement creates new revisions plus compatibility/readiness evidence; historical revisions never mutate
DV-7  sound processing that preserves acting/timing may remain downstream Sound Post; ADR/dialogue edits that change words/timing/acting re-enter A7 as a new Vocal Performance candidate
DV-8  dialogue/vocal identity is independent of Shot boundaries so J-cuts, L-cuts, overlap, off-screen speech, and multi-Shot segmentation remain representable
DV-9  an ad-lib that disagrees with the selected A1 line is not silently normalized by speech analysis; semantic revision/adoption or an explicit incompatibility is required
```

The Performance design gate is therefore a **co-design gate**: the first body/facial Performance representation cannot freeze independently of dialogue/vocal identity, timebase, synchronization, and replacement semantics. Full Foley, ambience, SFX, music, mixing, mastering, and delivery remain future Sound/Finishing domains.

Version 1.5 preserves every v1.4 authority owner and milestone boundary and adds a **future editorial/finishing preservation perimeter** derived from APR-121–124. The revision deliberately does not define a Sequence/Edit schema, transition model, timeline UI, NLE integration, mastering format, or new authority domain. It establishes only the invariants that future design must preserve:

```text
approved/select media remains immutable
editorial decisions reference exact retained source identities + temporal ranges
playback/proxy media never silently replaces source authority
production-property preservation and media preservation are separate axes
conform/materialization reports an explicit media-preservation class
executor commands/project files are execution provenance, not editorial authority
```

This clarification does not reorder M15→M16 or the post-M16 Performance program.

Version 1.6 preserves the v1.5 source/proxy/media-preservation perimeter and adds two future editorial invariants derived from APR-125–126:

```text
meaning-bearing editorial choices resolve deterministically before materialization planning
preview/review/final paths consume the same resolved editorial meaning
preservation conform and composition rendering are distinct replaceable materialization modes
materialization mode/executor changes cannot silently redefine source ranges, timing, transitions, graphics, or audio placement
resolved randomness/defaults/inference become explicit before historical editorial state is accepted
```

This revision still does **not** freeze a Sequence/Edit schema, a `ResolvedEditorialPlan` schema, a transition object model, a compositor, an NLE integration, or a delivery/mastering authority. G12 remains responsible for the exact persistent/editorial model.

